4.baseline:
Scope of Services and Deliverables.
(a) The Counterparty shall provide the Services and deliver the Deliverables to the Company strictly in accordance with:
  (i) this Agreement, including all Schedules;
  (ii) the applicable Statement of Work or Order Form executed by the Parties under this Agreement;
  (iii) the Service Levels, Specifications, Documentation and Acceptance Criteria incorporated in or attached to this Agreement;
  (iv) all Applicable Law and industry standards applicable to the Services and Deliverables; and
  (v) the Company's policies and standards expressly incorporated by reference in this Agreement.
(b) No variation without approval. The Counterparty shall not vary, reduce, expand, substitute, suspend or otherwise alter the scope, specification, quality, timing or manner of provision of any Service or Deliverable without the Company's prior written approval, and any variation shall be subject to Clause [●] (Change Control).
(c) No implied obligations. No obligation, warranty, representation, licence, right or authorisation is created by implication, estoppel, course of dealing or usage of trade. The Services and Deliverables are limited to those expressly described in this Agreement, and the Counterparty has no obligation to provide, and the Company no right to receive, any service, deliverable, support, update or enhancement not expressly set out in this Agreement.

4.buyside:
Enhanced Supplier Obligations. In addition to Clause [●] (Scope of Services and Deliverables), the Counterparty shall:
(a) provide the Services using personnel who (i) hold the qualifications, certifications, regulatory approvals and security clearances required by this Agreement, Applicable Law and industry standards; (ii) have undergone background and reference checks appropriate to the sensitivity of the Services; and (iii) have been trained on the security, data-protection, confidentiality and compliance obligations relevant to the Services;
(b) deliver each Deliverable by the date and in the format specified in the applicable Statement of Work or Order Form, and ensure each Deliverable meets the Acceptance Criteria and Specifications;
(c) notify the Company in writing within [forty-eight (48)] hours of becoming aware of any dependency, constraint or impediment that may delay or degrade any Service or Deliverable, and propose mitigation measures for the Company's approval;
(d) not reduce, discontinue, degrade, substitute, outsource or offshore any Service, Deliverable, personnel or methodology without the Company's prior written consent; and
(e) where a Milestone or delivery date is designated as critical or as one in respect of which time is of the essence, treat time as of the essence in respect of that Milestone.

4.sellside:
Limited Obligations. The Company's obligations under this Agreement are limited to those expressly set out in its operative clauses. The Company does not assume, and shall not be taken to have assumed, any:
(a) advisory, consultancy, suitability or financial-planning obligation;
(b) fiduciary, trustee, custodian, agency or broker duty;
(c) investment-management, portfolio-management or discretionary-trading obligation;
(d) obligation to monitor, supervise or conduct due diligence on the Counterparty's activities, decisions or transactions; or
(e) regulated activity or licensed function not expressly permitted by the Company's licences and agreed in this Agreement.
Exclusion of unstated expectations. Any feature, function, service, support, deliverable or performance level not expressly set out in this Agreement is excluded, and the Counterparty shall not rely on any oral representation, marketing material, demonstration, pilot or prior course of dealing as creating any such obligation.

4.fallback:
High-Level Scope (Low-Risk Engagements). The Services and Deliverables are described at a high level in Schedule [●], provided that:
(a) the principal deliverable or outcome is described with sufficient specificity to determine whether it has been delivered;
(b) the acceptance standard or test is stated;
(c) the Fees are fixed or subject to a stated not-to-exceed cap; and
(d) the Company may reject non-conforming work and withhold payment until conforming work is delivered.

2.baseline:
Definitions and Interpretation.
(a) Defined terms. Capitalised terms have the meanings given in Clause [●] (Definitions) or, where specified, in the relevant Schedule. Terms not defined have their ordinary meaning in the commercial context of this Agreement and, where applicable, accepted industry usage.
(b) Interpretation. Unless the context otherwise requires:
  (i) references to a Clause, Section or Schedule are to a clause, section or schedule of or to this Agreement;
  (ii) the singular includes the plural and vice versa, and any gender includes every gender;
  (iii) "include", "includes" and "including" are illustrative and do not limit the generality of the preceding words;
  (iv) headings are for convenience only and do not affect interpretation;
  (v) references to a statute or regulation include any subordinate legislation and any amendment, consolidation or re-enactment in force from time to time;
  (vi) "written" or "in writing" includes email and other electronic means capable of being read, stored and reproduced, unless a particular form of execution is expressly required; and
  (vii) references to "knowledge" or "awareness" mean the actual knowledge, after due enquiry, of the officers or senior managers of the relevant Party having direct responsibility for the relevant subject matter.

6.buyside:
Company Conditions Precedent. Without limiting Schedule [●], the Company is not required to perform any obligation (including payment) unless and until each of the following is satisfied to its reasonable satisfaction:
(a) execution and delivery by both Parties of this Agreement and all ancillary documents;
(b) completion of the Company's information-security due diligence, vendor risk assessment and (where applicable) penetration testing of the Counterparty's systems;
(c) verification that the Counterparty holds and maintains all licences, permits and authorisations required under Applicable Law to perform the Services, and is in good standing with all relevant Regulators;
(d) receipt of certificates of insurance complying with Clause [●] (Insurance); and
(e) where the Services involve Personal Data, completion to the Company's satisfaction of a data protection impact assessment.

6.sellside:
Counterparty Conditions Precedent. The Company's obligations to activate the Services, grant access to the Platform or commence provision are conditional on the Counterparty's prior satisfaction of each of the following:
(a) completion of all technical integration, configuration, testing and Documentation review specified in the Implementation Plan;
(b) completion, to the Company's reasonable satisfaction, of KYC/AML onboarding, including identity verification, beneficial-ownership and source-of-funds information;
(c) payment of all setup fees, deposits or upfront charges;
(d) written acceptance of all applicable product terms, acceptable-use policies and data-processing terms; and
(e) where the Counterparty is regulated or will use the Services for regulated activities, verification that it holds the necessary licences and approvals.

7.buyside:
Counterparty Implementation Obligations. The Counterparty shall:
(a) deliver each milestone and deliverable by the date specified in the Implementation Plan, and immediately notify the Company in writing of any actual or anticipated delay, with proposed remediation;
(b) provide the Company with all documentation, technical specifications, integration guides, test environments, sandbox access and support reasonably required for the Company to conduct thorough acceptance testing;
(c) remediate all defects, errors, security vulnerabilities and non-conformities identified by the Company in testing, and re-submit for testing within [●] Business Days of the Company's defect notice;
(d) provide a rollback plan approved in writing by the Company before any production deployment, specifying rollback triggers, procedures and timeline, data-recovery procedures, business-continuity measures and (where applicable) customer communications;
(e) not deploy, activate or release to production any Service, Deliverable, integration or configuration change without the Company's express prior written go-live approval for that deployment; and
(f) where implementation involves data migration, provide a data-migration plan approved by the Company, with data mapping, validation and reconciliation procedures.

7.sellside:
Counterparty Onboarding Obligations. The Counterparty shall complete all onboarding requirements before the Company activates the Services or grants access to the Platform, including:
(a) completion, to the Company's reasonable satisfaction, of all KYC/AML procedures, identity verification, beneficial-ownership disclosure and source-of-funds verification specified in the Company's onboarding procedures;
(b) completion of all technical integration requirements (API configuration, credential setup, webhook endpoints, IP whitelisting and other prerequisites) specified in the Documentation;
(c) completion of user acceptance testing in the Company's sandbox and written confirmation that the Counterparty has completed testing to its satisfaction;
(d) written acceptance of all applicable Company product terms, acceptable-use policies and service-level terms governing use of the Platform; and
(e) payment of all setup, onboarding or deposit amounts.
Right to delay activation. The Company may, in its sole discretion, delay or withhold activation, access or go-live pending satisfaction of the onboarding requirements, completion of its internal readiness reviews, or resolution of any security, compliance, operational or technical concern, in each case without liability to the Counterparty for the delay.

7.fallback:
Deemed Acceptance (Limited). Where deemed acceptance is commercially unavoidable, the following applies:
(a) the acceptance-testing period shall be not less than [ten (10)] Business Days following delivery, extended by [five (5)] Business Days for each rejection and re-submission cycle;
(b) the Company may reject any Deliverable or milestone by written notice specifying the defects with reasonable particularity, and the Counterparty shall remediate and re-submit;
(c) deemed acceptance applies only to minor, non-critical defects that do not materially affect core functionality, security, data integrity, regulatory compliance or the Company's intended use; and
(d) deemed acceptance does not waive the Company's rights to claim breach of warranty, require remediation of latent defects discovered after acceptance, or terminate for material breach.

